Objective
The objective of this program is to implement the Breadth-First Search (BFS) algorithm to determine the connectivity of farm fields in an irrigation system. Each farm field is represented as a vertex, and each irrigation channel is represented as an edge in a graph. The BFS algorithm starts from the field connected to the water source and visits all reachable fields level by level using a queue. After traversal, the program identifies and displays the fields that cannot be reached from the water source. This helps to identify disconnected fields in the irrigation network.
